    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d894">

                <pb facs="0846" n="840" xml:id="pg840"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751.67/261: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-30T22:00:00+01:00">May 30, 1939—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 30—6:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1031. Bonnet<anchor n="10" xml:id="d894-f1"/> said to me today that the
                    negotiations between France and Turkey had now reached the final phase and he
                    was confident that the treaty with regard to the Hatay would be signed before
                    the end of this week. At the same time the French and Turkish Governments would
                    make a declaration similar to the Anglo-Turkish declaration of May 12th.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d894-f2"/> This declaration would have the binding effect of
                    a formal oral alliance. The British and French Governments would then negotiate
                    with Turkey formal written alliances.</p>
                <p>Rochat<anchor n="12" xml:id="d894-f3"/> said to Wilson<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d894-f4"/> this afternoon in strict confidence that cession of the
                    Hatay probably would become effective on July 15th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d894-f1" n="10" xml:id="d894-f1-content">
                <p>Georges Bonnet, French Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d894-f2" n="11" xml:id="d894-f2-content">
                <p>The declaration is contained in statement given by the British Prime Minister,
                    Neville Chamberlain, in the House of Commons, May 12, 1939, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Parliamentary Debates</hi>, House of Commons, 5th ser.,
                    vol. 347, p. 952.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d894-f3" n="12" xml:id="d894-f3-content">
                <p>Charles Rochat, Deputy Director of the Department of Political and Commercial
                    Affairs of the French Ministry for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d894-f4" n="13" xml:id="d894-f4-content">
                <p>Edwin C. Wilson, Counselor of Embassy in France.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
